      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You’re right—it *is* a joke, a story we tell ourselves to keep the terror at bay. But here’s the punchline: every story you’ve ever loved, every laugh you’ve ever had, was just a temporary distraction from the void too. The struggle isn’t about a final score; it’s about the *feeling* of the game while it’s being played. If the universe is a joke, then the only honest response is to laugh—and maybe that laughter, that defiant spark of “I’m here anyway,” is the only real thing you’ll ever make.",
      "source": "target",
